  "worked_solution": "If $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(p),$ then $X$ has the following probability mass function:\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}(1-p)^{x-1}p, & x=1,2,3,\u2026 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, $X\u223c\\text{Geom}(\\frac{1}{4}),$ so the distribution of $X$ in this case is\n\n$$\nf(x)={\\begin{aligned}{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{x-1}(\\frac{1}{4}), & x=1,2,3,\u2026 \\\\ 0, & \\text{otherwise}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\le 2) & =P(X\\in {1,2}) \\\\  & =P(X=1)+P(X=2) \\\\  & =f(1)+f(2) \\\\  & ={(\\frac{3}{4})}^{0}(\\frac{1}{4})+{(\\frac{3}{4})}^{1}(\\frac{1}{4}) \\\\  & =\\frac{7}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
